<clickhouse>
    <!--
         Memory tuning for the lite (self-host) deployment ONLY: mounted by
         docker-compose.lite.yml, never by the full docker-compose.yml.

         (Note for editors, same as keeper.xml: XML comments may not contain a
         double hyphen, so this file uses colons and parentheses instead of
         the dash style used elsewhere in the repo.)

         The full stack's clickhouse/config.d/ has no memory settings at all,
         so ClickHouse runs on stock cache defaults sized for a server that
         expects to own the whole machine. Measured on this project's local
         stack: about 978 MiB idle, almost entirely those default caches
         rather than data actually held in memory. There is no schema or
         workload reason a single-tenant install needs gigabyte-scale
         mark/uncompressed caches.

         MEASURED, not a starting-point guess anymore: the original 768 MiB
         cap here was never actually checked against a real container, and it
         was wrong (`system.asynchronous_metrics`'s MemoryResident sat at
         ~833 MiB at idle, even with the reduced 128/64 MiB caches below):
         above the cap before any query ever ran. Every query, including a
         trivial one against a 178-row table, hit MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED via
         the OvercommitTracker as a result. 1536 MiB leaves real headroom
         above that measured idle floor for actual query execution, not just
         enough to sit idle.

         max_server_memory_usage is an explicit cap rather than 0 (auto
         detect from host RAM), because a self-hoster's Docker host is
         frequently shared with other things, and ClickHouse guessing from
         total host memory is the wrong default on a machine it does not own
         alone.
    -->
    <max_server_memory_usage>1610612736</max_server_memory_usage> <!-- 1536 MiB -->
    <mark_cache_size>134217728</mark_cache_size>                  <!-- 128 MiB (default is multi GiB) -->
    <uncompressed_cache_size>67108864</uncompressed_cache_size>   <!-- 64 MiB -->
</clickhouse>
